re else already ?"],["d84b063c_aa18ea41",5,-15,1,"nit: If you flip the cases it would make it easier to tell from the diff that the current behavior is not changed when this feature is disabled."],["e99b2eb5_63e6de04",5,-15,1,"Can this be null?"],["8cc3de20_be917854",5,-11,1,"I think we need to update the description of this CL slightly. This still only trims on moderate memory pressure, the key change from this experiment is that it will allow trimming of visible windows…"]],0,184],[7873843,20599,24,0.737,0.556,[[6,24]],[],0,185],[7873842,20599,86,2.361,1.866,[[6,0.956,25,84],[17,0.044,9,2]],[],0,186],[7849293,20605,21,0.737,0.556,[[6,0.696,26,15],[16,0.304,20,6]],[["1051a831_e15bfd92",6,-18,1,"nit: since IsChangeUnfocusedPriorityEnabled() is only used here, you could just do the check directly in this if statement"],["067c99c5_1b3eb545",1,-17,0,"is this really better? before we had a list of things to resolve for !desktop. now this hides it within the codebas"]],0,187],[7855781,20605,28,0.737,0.556,[[6,0.613,27,18],[19,0.258,9,7],[16,0.129,21,3]],[["c88ec19e_fbb8f7a1",7,-14,1,"Given that isDesktop() is strongly discouraged, is it possible to swap it out based on device capability? e.g.…"],["ef92238f_0b5341e8",7,-14,0,"nit: can this check for `sProtectRecentlyVisibleTab` be removed? Looks like it is set to TRUE for desktop builds... that probably needs to be cleaned up anyways."]],0,188],[7893747,20607,30,0.737,0.556,[[6,0.559,28,18],[19,0.235,10,7],[16,0.118,22,3],[17,0.088,10,2]],[],0,189],[7894715,20607,12,0.421,0.3,[[6,29]],[],0,190],[7884754,20608,265,7.601,6.192,[[6,0.828,30,222],[24,0.172,1,43]],[["bbf16821_2d69446c",8,-3,0,"The old logic did not check for base::android::device_info::is_desktop(). Is that intended?"],["d9561e50_dc61c7cc",9,-3,0,"pre-existing bug, but can you change this to use `new_page_node` please if that's not too much trouble?"]],0,191],[7900202,20608,2,0.143,0.09,[[6,31]],[],0,192],[7906769,20615,52,1.341,1.058,[[6,32]],[["baed23f1_6c29